{
  "rules": [
    "Apply a strong negative bias correction (-15% to -20%) to the model's 30-day forecast when recent history shows a downtrend (price decline) despite neutral sentiment, as models consistently overshoot recovery.",
    "Detect 'overshoot' patterns where the model predicts a steady rise after a price spike; correct by reducing the forecast trajectory by 10-15% to account for mean reversion volatility.",
    "When sentiment history shows a single -1.00 spike followed by neutral values, assume the model ignores this negative signal and reduce the forecast floor by approximately 8-10 EUR.",
    "Reduce forecast confidence in the first 7 days of the horizon if the immediate past 3 days show high volatility (range >5 EUR), as models tend to smooth out sharp corrections.",
    "If the current price is near a local minimum and sentiment is neutral, cap the upward forecast at the average of the last 10 days rather than allowing full model extrapolation."
  ]
}
